-O, -OO, PYTHONOPTIMIZE; py-os-1124): the compiler's level for every"] [217 1 "// source the runtime compiles (compileSource's mode +opt1 or +opt2: asserts left out and __debug__ False from 1,"] [218 1 "// docstrings left out from 2, as codegen does), sys.flags.optimize and builtins.__debug__."] [229 1 "// OptimizeLevel is optimizeLevel for the host (arbace.python's start: the main module compiled at it)."] [232 1 "// optMode is a compile mode at optimization level n (py-os-1124): the mode itself under 1, else with +opt1 or +opt2 (the"] [233 1 "// host's compile-source binds the compiler's level from it; the IR cache keys the whole mode)."] [244 1 "// dontWriteBytecode is config's write_bytecode negated (-B, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE; py-os-1124): sys.flags'"] [245 1 "// dont_write_bytecode. pyi writes no bytecode cache at import in any case (sys.dont_write_bytecode stays True: its IR"] [246 1 "// cache is the host's)."] [251 1 "// startInspect is -i (bin/pyi python's PYI_INSPECT, queue 289, read once and removed from the environment as"] [252 1 "// PYI_SAFE_PATH is): 0 without it, 1 for -i, 2 for -i with no code to run (CPython's REPL on stdin, its banner but"] [253 1 "// under -q), and 2 or 3 too for no code on a terminal without -i (queue 313, pymain_run_stdin's stdin_is_interactive:"] [254 1 "// startInspectOption false). PYTHONINSPECT at start (but under -E or -I) sets sys.flags.inspect, not interactive, as"] [255 1 "// config's inspect."] [280 2 "// inspectTTY: the REPL is the run because stdin is a terminal, not -i (sys.flags' inspect and interactive 0)"] [284 1 "// startInspectOption is whether -i was given (config's inspect and interactive)."] [287 1 "// inspectAfter is pymain_repl's test (Modules/main.c): the REPL after the main module when -i was given or"] [288 1 "// PYTHONINSPECT is set (at start, or in the environment the program leaves), stdin a terminal or -i given."] [297 1 "// endMain is the main module's end with its status: Py_FinalizeEx's, or unde